# Build context exclusions for the Dockerfile.
#
# Everything here is either regenerated inside the builder stage or never read
# by it. The two that matter are .git (largest single tree) and the Git LFS
# example data: the build reads neither, and shipping the context across to the
# daemon is otherwise the slowest step of a CI image build.
.git/

# Host build trees and virtualenv. .venv especially: the builder creates its
# own at /opt/q3-src/.venv, and a host venv copied over it carries absolute
# paths from another machine that break every interpreter shebang in it.
build/
build_*/
.venv/
node_modules/

# Example inputs and pseudopotential data are read from the host at run time
# (bind-mounted by apptainer/podman-hpc/shifter), never from inside the image.
examples/

# Container artifacts, so a local `apptainer build` result never re-enters the
# context of the next image build.
*.sif
